# UI backend — SAMPLE, no real secrets (ARD §13)
DATA_ROOT=/path/to/data-repo
# where the frozen JSON schemas live (code-repo/schemas), for the engine CLIs
SCHEMA_DIR=/path/to/code-repo/schemas
# The operational store: accounts, roles, scopes, sessions and the activity
# record. There is no user credential in this file any more — people are rows in
# app.db, and the first Editor is created by `inja-seed`
# (docs/runbooks/06-changing-users.md).
#
# Point this OUTSIDE DATA_ROOT — the app refuses to start if it is inside, and
# says so by name. The operational store must never enter the
# data-repo working tree: it would be committed and pushed to GitHub by git-push,
# taking every password hash and session with it. Unset, the default is
# `DATA_ROOT/../app.db`, which is beside the data-repo for a host run but is the
# container's throwaway layer under Docker — the compose files set it explicitly
# to /state/app.db on the ui-state volume.
APP_DB=/path/to/app.db
# secret for signing the session cookie
SESSION_SIGNING_KEY=
# session lifetime in seconds (default 86400)
SESSION_TTL=86400
# How many reverse proxies stand in front of this process. It decides which
# X-Forwarded-For entry is recorded as the client address in the session row and
# in the activity record: with 1, the last entry — the one Caddy appended and
# therefore the only one a client cannot write. 0 (the default) ignores the header
# and records the TCP peer, which is what a host run without a proxy needs. Set it
# to 1 wherever deploy/Caddyfile is in front; leave it 0 if this process is reached
# directly, or a caller can dictate the address the audit record blames.
TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=0
# built frontend directory (ui/dist); may be absent until Phase 6
UI_STATIC_DIR=
# Where generated export documents are written. Unset = the export feature is off
# (the endpoint answers 503 and the UI says so). In Docker this is supplied by the
# compose file (`EXPORT_DIR: /exports`, on the ui-exports volume) — leave it blank
# here. For a host run, point it at a directory you can write to, or leave it unset.
EXPORT_DIR=
# The one shared login that opens a published export (/exports/...). Separate from
# the UI users above on purpose: it opens exports and nothing else. Both blank =
# the gate is CLOSED: /exports answers 401 to everyone except a signed-in UI user,
# and no login form is offered. There is no fallback to open access.
#
# **LEAVE BOTH UNSET. This is a decision, not an omission.** A caller holding this
# credential carries no identity, so `routers/export_files.py::_authorise` has no
# scope to re-derive and no role to read a capability from: they are served EVERY
# department's exports and are asked for no capability, which is the one hole left
# in D12's two-part gate. Spec D24 (sub-project P2) retires the credential
# outright and is what closes it. Until then, unset is the configuration that has
# no hole in it, and it costs nothing — everyone reads exports through their own
# account, which is where scope and `export_pdf` are actually enforced.
#
# `docs/runbooks/02-secrets-and-auth.md` still carries the command that generates
# the hash. That is there for whoever reverses this decision deliberately; it is
# not a step in a normal deploy.
EXPORT_USERNAME=
# argon2 hash of the export password (never the plaintext) — see above before
# filling this in, and docs/runbooks/02-secrets-and-auth.md for the command
EXPORT_PASSWORD_HASH=
# Where the built export templates live. Owned by the image — the Dockerfile sets
# it to /app/ui-export-templates. Leave blank so the image stays the single source
# of truth; only set it for a host run without Docker (then: ui/dist-export).
UI_EXPORT_TEMPLATE_DIR=
# The browser that prints each export to a PDF beside its HTML. Owned by the image
# too — the Dockerfile installs Debian `chromium` and sets this to
# /usr/lib/chromium/chromium. Leave blank; only set it for a host run, and only to
# a Chromium that supports CDP Page.printToPDF (Debian's `chromium-shell` does
# not). Unset simply means exports get no PDF; nothing else changes.
CHROMIUM_PATH=
# author identity for ui-edit commits
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=ui-edit
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=ui-edit@inja.local
